body:
> That way you can do general setup and have some more specific setup in some places.

@jhli I opt for merging then. If you really want/need it to completely overwrite it, removing the behavior first would be the way to go. And then you would need the additional overhead of checking if it existed before.
But: Don't we usually have a param for merging vs overwriting? Which would probably simplify it.

@markstory Looking at the code it will still produce awkward results in some cases this way, though.

```
public function __construct(Table $table, array $config = []) {
    $config += ... // !!!
    $this->config($config);
}
```

All configs dynamically added through constructor will be lost with a config() overwrite.
In this case using addBehavior() to overwrite it would be more correct as it triggers a complete re-setup including constructor call. We should then not use config() with overwrite here, and only use config() for merging/adjusting the configs.
